## Original Content
Voters in at least six states will soon decide ballot measures related to voter ID — the largest number of voter ID measures in a single year. The tally includes three prominent swing states.

## Summary
Voters in at least six states, including three swing states, will decide on voter ID ballot measures this year, marking the highest number of such measures in a single year. The outcome could significantly impact political landscapes and election integrity in key regions.

## Key Points
- At least six states have voter ID ballot measures scheduled for this year.
- This is the largest number of voter ID measures in a single year to date.
- Three of the states are prominent swing states, highlighting potential national political implications.


